On the sides of a unit square, right-angled triangles are constructed outward on the hypotenuses. Let $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ be the vertices of their right angles, and $O_{1}, O_{2}, O_{3}$, and $O_{4}$ be the centers of the incircles of these triangles. Prove that:

a) The area of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ does not exceed 2;

b) The area of the quadrilateral $O_{1}O_{2}O_{3}O_{4}$ does not exceed 1.

A city has $n$ bus lines satisfying the following conditions:
(1) Any bus stop is serviced by at most 3 bus lines;
(2) Any bus line has at least two stops;
(3) For any two specific bus lines, there is a third line such that passengers can transfer from either of the two specified lines to the other through this third line.

Prove that the number of bus stops is at least $\frac{5}{6}(n-5)$.

Let \( f:[0,1] \rightarrow \mathbb{R} \) be a function satisfying:
1. \( f(x) \geq 0 \) for all \( x \in [0,1] \);
2. \( f(1) = 1 \);
3. \( f(x) + f(y) \leq f(x+y) \) for all \( x, y \) such that \( x+y \in [0,1] \).

Find the smallest constant \( c \) such that \( f(x) \leq c x \) for all \( x \in [0,1] \) and prove your conclusion.

Given \( a_{1}=1 \) and \( a_{2}=2 \),
\[ a_{n+2}=\left\{\begin{array}{ll}
5a_{n+1}-3a_{n}, & \text{if } a_{n}a_{n+1} \text{ is even}; \\
a_{n+1}-a_{n}, & \text{if } a_{n}a_{n+1} \text{ is odd}
\end{array}\right. \]

Prove that for all \( n \in \mathbf{N} \), \( a_{n} \neq 0 \).

Let \( O_1 \) and \( O_2 \) be the first and second centers of rotation of triangle \( ABC \), and \( O \) be the center of the circumscribed circle. Prove that:

a) \( \angle O_1 AB = \angle O_2 BC = \angle O_1 CA = \angle O_2 BA = \angle O_2 CB = \angle O_2 AC \);

b) \( O_1 \) coincides with \( O_2 \) if and only if triangle \( ABC \) is equilateral;

c) \( O_1 \) and \( O_2 \) are equidistant from \( O: O_1O = O_2O \);

d) The common value of the angles \( \angle O_1 AB, \angle O_1 BC, \angle O_1 CA, \angle O_2 BA, \angle O_2 CB, \angle O_2 AC \) does not exceed \( 30^\circ \); furthermore, \( \varphi = 30^\circ \) if and only if triangle \( ABC \) is equilateral.

