Given the function \( f(x) \) is defined on \( (-1,1) \), \( f\left(\frac{1}{2}\right)=-1 \), and satisfies \( f(x)+f(y)=f\left(\frac{x+y}{1+x y}\right) \) for \( x, y \in(-1,1) \). Prove that:
