(2) Find the value of \(AQ \cdot BQ\).

Let \( A = \{x \mid 0 \leqslant x \leqslant 1\} \), and let \( f \) be a mapping from \( A \) to the set of real numbers \( \mathbf{R} \), satisfying:
(1) \( f(1) = 1 \);
(2) \( f(x) \geqslant 0 \) for all \( x \in A \);
(3) If \( x, y, x + y \in A \), then \( f(x + y) \geqslant f(x) + f(y) \).

Prove: For any \( x \in A \), \( f(x) \leqslant 2x \).

